# Copy to `.dev.vars` for `wrangler dev` (git-ignored). In production these are set with
# `wrangler secret put <NAME>` instead of living in a file.

# Signs node tokens and link codes. Use a long random value: `openssl rand -hex 32`.
ROUTER_SECRET="dev-only-change-me"

# Gates POST /register -- a node holds this too (see docs/channels.md §8 for why that's
# acceptable), it is not browser-facing. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
ROUTER_ADMIN_SECRET="dev-only-change-me-too"

# The one Telegram bot ADI runs (api.telegram.org -> BotFather). TELEGRAM_SECRET_TOKEN is the
# `secret_token` set on this bot's `setWebhook` call, echoed back as
# X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token on every delivery -- that header, not an HMAC, is Telegram's
# whole webhook-authenticity story.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=""
TELEGRAM_SECRET_TOKEN=""

# The one Slack app ADI runs (api.slack.com/apps -> create from slack-manifest.yaml). Unlike
# Telegram's single bot token, these are the *app's* OAuth credentials -- the bot token itself is
# per-workspace, minted at "Add to Slack" time and held encrypted in that connection's own
# Durable Object, never here. SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET verifies X-Slack-Signature on every webhook.
SLACK_CLIENT_ID=""
SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET=""
SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=""
